{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01G897yhESa4jivLKBDK7ycd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **Q27: What is positional encoding and why is it needed?** (`answers/01-027-what-is-positional-encoding-and-why-is-it-needed.md`).\n\nKey content covered:\n- **Root cause**: self-attention is permutation-invariant — tokens \"dog bites man\" and \"man bites dog\" produce identical attention scores without position signals\n- **Evolution**: sinusoidal (Vaswani 2017, fixed formulas) → learned absolute (BERT/GPT-2, embedding table, hard context cap) → **RoPE** (Llama 2/3, Mistral, GPT-4 — rotate Q/K vectors so attention depends on relative distance only)\n- **Production angle**: RoPE's relative-distance property is why Llama 2 could be extended from 4K → 100K context by changing one hyperparameter (θ base from 10K → 500K), with no new parameters\n- **ALiBi** mentioned as an alternative (MPT-7B) that adds distance-proportional negative bias to attention logits\n- 3 pitfalls: stopping at the 2017 answer, confusing encoding vs bias, skipping the permutation-invariance explanation\n\nNext up: **Q28 — MMLU, BigBench, HumanEval — what does each measure? Limitations?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":306,"cache_read_input_tokens":57277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":306,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de0232fa-5417-41c9-a9a0-1be80977bce2","uuid":"a1720839-50ea-42e0-85c3-5dc2b1e76538"}
